WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:02.970
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.980
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.750
How have y'all been?

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:09.360
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:09.360
<b>K</b>

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:11.100
Today, my very own new TV series, 
<i>Kero-chan's Eat Till You Drop</i>, begins!

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.110
<b>That show doesn't exist! 
Follow the script!</b>

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.940
This'll be a special presentation to 
review what's happened so far.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:35.010
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:35.010
<b>K</b>

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.440
It all started when Sakura found 
an old book in her dad's library.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.760
Inside the book were Clow Cards 
that possessed magical power.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.040
And Sakura accidentally activated 
them, so they scattered.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.860
And so, Cardcaptor Sakura was 
born to retrieve all the cards.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.460
This is her friend Tomoyo...

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.630
She's the one who always 
makes Sakura's costumes.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.150
And this is the kid from Hong Kong,

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.600
and he and Sakura like each other, and, um...

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.010
<b>Don't rush so much!</b>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.300
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.300
<b>K</b>

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.800
Anyway, let's get to it!

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.000
<i>Cardcaptor Sakura: Clear Card</i> starts now!

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:22.020
<i>When all the cards have gathered together...</i>

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.690
<i>It is not the end, but rather, the beginning.</i>

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.280
<i>The beginning of the end...</i>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.010
<b>Sakura and the Clear Cards</b>

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.420
It's just about time to go, Sakura!

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.490
Okay!

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.600
<i>My name is Sakura Kinomoto.</i>

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.800
<i>I just started my first year 
at Tomoeda Middle School.</i>

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.110
I don't even see any bedhead. 
Lookin' sharp...

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.520
I like!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.310
Thanks, Kero-chan.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.490
I was just about to call for you.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:10.940
It's almost time...

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.050
<b>Stare</b>

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.050
D-Do I look weird?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:18.730
Not at all.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:23.300
I was just thinking, it wasn't so long ago that 
you were wearing the elementary uniform.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.470
The middle school uniform suits you 
well, too. You look very cute!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.790
Right, Toya-kun?

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.590
So even monsters wear costumes.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.100
Excuse me?!

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.680
It's not a costume! It's my uniform!

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.310
But you don't deny being a monster?

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.800
You might be in college now, 
but you're still just a kid!

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.320
Well, you might be in middle school, 
but you're still a brat.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.320
<b>Now, now...</b>

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.320
<b>Grrr!</b>

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.080
Sakura-san, you'd better get going.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.550
I'm heading out now, Mom.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.690
Be careful.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:57.640
I will!

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.640
It's so pretty!

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:13.590
The cherry blossoms were still just buds 
during our entrance ceremony.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.520
We should all have a flower-viewing party.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.100
I'll talk to Tomoyo-chan about it.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.910
I wish I could have seen this 
with Syaoran-kun, too...

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.610
I promise I'll come back someday,

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:38.620
after I finish what I need to do in Hong Kong.

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.400
Can I name this bear "Syaoran"?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.320
Sure.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:00.140
<i>Syaoran-kun is working hard in Hong Kong.</i>

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.470
<i>I'll work hard, too!</i>

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.440
Okay, our classes begin today.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:11.540
Now that you're in middle school, 
if you're struggling with anything,

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.470
you can talk to me, your homeroom teacher, 
or my assistant, Mori-sensei.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:16.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.500
I'm so glad I get to sit next 
to you, Tomoyo-chan!

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.500
I'm glad, too.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.460
Even Chiharu-chan is in our class again.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.050
Yeah.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.540
One in every ten thousand 
cornstalks grows a cow.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.540
Naoko-chan and Yamazaki-kun 
are in the class next door,

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.920
but they're still in the same school.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.920
And that cow becomes corned—

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:39.360
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.240
Rika-chan went to another school,

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.350
but we can still call and e-mail her.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.490
We should all go out together again, sometime.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.360
Yeah!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.190
Next.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.030
You're amazing, Sakura-chan!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.860
Just like always!

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.580
Thanks.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.950
My name is Mike. I'm from Portland.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:05:59.960
<b>Fluent</b>

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.710
<b>Middle School Math</b>

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.460
<b>Inequality Sign     Absolute Value 

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.600
What did you think of first period?

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.710
It was so hard!

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:12.990
But I'm gonna try hard to make friends 
with math in middle school.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:13.710
English, too.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.650
I'll be rooting for you.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.290
Syaoran-kun...

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.270
I finally finished my business in Hong Kong.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:06.590
Now I can stay in Tomoeda forever.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.420
Really?

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:09.520
Yeah.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:13.770
I don't have to settle for letters 
and phone calls anymore?

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.150
Yeah.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.610
Now we can be together forever!

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:21.870
Yeah.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:28.630
There's so much I wanted to tell 
you when I saw you again!

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:29.620
Me, too.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.130
Tell me... All of it.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:33.550
Sure.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.050
Don't mind me.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:48.700
I got the cutest footage of 
you today, Sakura-chan!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.030
You haven't changed a bit, Daidouji.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.110
Oh, yeah. What about school?

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.440
I'm starting at Tomoeda Middle School tomorrow.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:58.790
Really?

00:07:58.790 --> 00:07:59.750
Yeah.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.310
I hope we'll all be in the same class.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:02.950
Yeah!

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.840
But it's okay if we're not.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:07.960
I can still be right beside you.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.320
Sakura...

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.390
<b>Stare</b>

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.630
W-Well, I'd... I'd better hurry home!

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.150
Yeah! Syaoran-kun!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:30.190
He's starting at Tomoeda 
Middle School tomorrow.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.230
That's wonderful.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:33.090
Yeah!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.620
Please send me a picture of you all together.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.940
I always look forward to those.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:43.320
Same here! I always look forward 
to your pictures of England!

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.910
Mizuki-sensei's, too!

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.540
<b>Sakura Kinomoto</b>

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.540
<b>

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.080
You heard her.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.880
Same goes for me.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.340
I always look forward to your pictures 
and letters, Sakura-chan.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:55.470
Mizuki-sensei!

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.340
If you take some more nice 
ones, send them over.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:08:59.290
I will!

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.280
I'll send you some delicious tea soon.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:02.850
Thank you!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.630
She's been looking at me all this time, 
as if she wanted to talk to you.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.730
You two are so close!

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:15.900
And soon, you'll be able to see the one 
you want to be closer to any time.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.380
Yeah.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.160
<b>Eriol-kun</b>

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.160
<b>
End Call</b>

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:21.340
I bet you'll have a lovely dream tonight.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:26.660
You said you hadn't had many dreams lately, right?

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.660
Y-Yeah...

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.170
Because I've been so busy, I guess.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:38.180
<b>
Eriol-kun</b>

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:38.180
<b>
End Call</b>

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:34.300
What matters most is that 
you're healthy and energetic.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:36.680
Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.000
Well, goodnight.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.170
Tell Cerberus I said hello.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:40.190
Take that! And that! And that!

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.870
Goodnight.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.680
Yes! I beat the mid-boss!

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:47.740
Eriol-kun said to tell you hello.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:47.740
How's that? Did ya get 
a taste of my power?!

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:50.680
Oh, tell him to send us 
somethin' tasty again!

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.180
We already hung up...

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.990
I'll send him an e-mail later, then!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.990
I should write Spinny, too.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.110
<b>Kee-hee-hee</b>

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:00.220
I gotta send him a picture from that 
dessert buffet we went to the other day!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.700
<b>Kee-hee-hee</b>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:09:59.950
<b>Kee-hee-hee</b>

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:04.030
Which picture should I send? 
This one? Or maybe this one?

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:05.780
This one looks delicious!

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:10.720
Hey, isn't this the teddy 
bear ya gave that kid?

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.770
The one ya stayed up all night to make, 
before he went home to Hong Kong.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.850
What's it doin' here?

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.340
U-Um...

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.600
Thanks for walking me home.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.850
I know it was out of your way...

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.250
I wanted to stay together a bit longer.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.970
Oh, right. Here.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:40.870
This Sakura stayed by my side the whole time.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.530
My Syaoran-kun bear did, too!

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.740
He stayed with me the whole time!

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:53.420
I think she was lonely, being separated 
from the one who made her.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.590
Would you stay with her for a little while?

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.480
Sure!

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.730
Oh, but in that case,

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.870
the Syaoran-kun bear probably 
wants to see his maker, too!

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.270
Yeah, I guess so.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.810
Let's trade them for a while, then.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:11.720
Okay!

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.530
<b>I Am a Stuffed Animal</b>

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.530
Come in.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.570
Welcome home.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:22.390
Thanks.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.650
It's from Yuki.

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:29.430
He said he found it at the 
general store he works at.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.280
I'll send him an e-mail to thank him!

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.160
Sure. Get to bed soon.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.160
Okay!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:36.960
<b>I Am a Stuffed Animal</b>

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.050
<b>Stuffed Animal Undone</b>

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.740
So Yukibunny wasn't with him today?

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:43.400
I guess not.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.340
If he'd stayed overnight, I could 
have thanked him in person.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.770
I haven't used this in a long time...

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.880
But I know it's better that way.

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.000
Cards?

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.710
They're clear...

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:41.080
Who is that?

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.220
Are you...

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:15.570
What the heck's wrong, Sakura?

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.320
Sakura-chan!

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:40.200
Yukito-san...

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:44.080
Good morning. What brings 
you over so early?

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.370
This is an emergency!

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:51.500
Come in.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:53.960
I'll change now.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:10.950
What happened?

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.450
What is this?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.560
I had a dream last night.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.790
Clear cards were floating all around me,

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.760
and then they shattered.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.870
I got worried and opened the 
Book of the Clow Cards...

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:27.110
And all of the cards had become clear.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:31.890
I don't sense any magical power.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:33.820
I didn't, either.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.180
And the key?

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:38.620
<i>Release!</i>

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:48.190
So this means Sakura hasn't 
lost her magical power...

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.880
Were the shattering cards 
all you saw in the dream?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.240
Someone was standing there.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:55.320
Who?

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:59.140
They were wearing some kind of hood

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.660
that covered their face and everything else.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.690
Do you feel anything?

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:05.790
Not a thing.

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:11.420
Yukibunny's gotta go to school, too.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.870
I'll stick with Sakura for a while.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.470
But...

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:19.050
I don't know why this happened yet.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:26.470
So I want Yukito-san to go about 
his life as normally as possible.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.720
Yukito doesn't retain any memories of this form,

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.680
but he is perceptive.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:38.400
Not informing him may only 
make him worry more.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.780
If it does, I'll tell him myself.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.170
But until then...

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.610
I promise.

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:53.220
And since Syaoran-kun is back 
now, I'll talk to him about it.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.220
Make sure you tell him...

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:00.230
Even the smallest things.

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:03.940
Okay!

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:06.400
The cards?

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:09.340
Yue didn't know why, either.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.520
Hey, kid, what d'you think?

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.530
I don't know.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:18.430
But whoever you saw in your 
dream must be connected.

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.840
You couldn't see their face, could you?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.570
No...

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.980
I went ahead and sent an e-mail to England.

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:29.960
Then, if something does happen...

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:34.600
It's the triumphant return 
of Cardcaptor Sakura!

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:34.600
Tomoyo-chan...

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.740
I've only seen you in ordinary clothes lately.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:40.710
It was making me a little depressed.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.720
<b>H-Huh? Ordinary?</b>

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:46.380
But in anticipation of something like this, 
I always have a stock of costumes ready,

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.800
and it's their time to shine, at last!

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:51.330
You've got some for me, too, right?!

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:52.600
But of course!

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.370
Oh, we need to get to class quickly.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.190
Yeah.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:00.950
Syaoran-kun...

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:03.700
Sorry I worried you.

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:05.870
Don't worry about it.

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.370
S-See you at lunch!

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.130
You brought up the costumes 
on purpose, didn't you?

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:17.940
So that Sakura wouldn't have to worry more.

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.770
It's because I believe in her.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:28.700
Sakura-chan has Kero-chan, Yue-san, 
her father, her brother,

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:31.200
all of our friends in England,

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.150
and...

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:36.050
She has you, Li-kun!

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.170
See you soon.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.360
Hey, Li-kun starts today, right?

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:42.890
Yeah.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.600
Why don't we all eat lunch together?

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.290
I brought some sweets I made.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:49.420
I love your sweets, Chiharu-chan!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:53.540
Yamazaki-kun is so lucky he gets to eat 
such delicious sweets all the time.

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.040
It's not <i>all</i> the time!

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.980
I'm a little worried about Li-kun, though...

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:04.590
He's in Class 3 with
Yamazaki-kun and Naoko-chan.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:09.000
Are you familiar with the school yet?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.860
Well, I'm just starting today.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.860
<b>Been a long time</b>

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.670
Speaking of "familiar"...

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:15.760
The word began with a fictional 
creature called "Familiar."

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:17.950
Is that something like Baku?

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:18.690
Right, right.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.520
And Familiar is a really friendly creature.

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:25.790
He only said things like "No walls between 
us, right?" and "We're friends, right?"

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:29.900
And that's where we got words like 
"familiar," and even "family."

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.950
I think I've read about that before...

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:35.450
I never knew! Thanks for telling me!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.820
Never change, Li-kun.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:40.840
Yeah.

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:43.840
Did they reply yet?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.360
No.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:48.910
Well, there's a time difference... 
Just give 'em a little longer.

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:51.190
Okay. Thanks, Kero-chan.

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:56.150
Sure! Feel free to give me more 
snacks tomorrow, to thank me!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.230
Okay. Let's make some together.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.330
Score!

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.770
Well, with that settled, let's get to sleep.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.640
Sweet dreams, Sakura.

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.040
Same to you, Kero-chan.

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:15.370
<i>Goodnight, Syaoran-kun.</i>

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:26.850
Who... are you?

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.100
A key?

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:42.110
Sakura!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.550
You were havin' a nightmare! Are you okay?

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.040
A... dream...

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:56.280
Sakura, is this...

00:20:57.200 --> 00:21:00.420
It's the key... from my dream.

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:04.890
Why is it here?

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.120
Still no reply from Eriol?

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:11.900
No.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:18.170
Kero-chan, you didn't feel anything 
bad last night, did you?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:22.420
No, I didn't notice a thing until 
your whimpering woke me up.

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:28.390
Watch out!

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:31.930
What is this?!

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.610
I don't know... I don't sense any presence.

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:37.270
But this is no ordinary wind!

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:42.720
Sakura! The cards!

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:43.660
Oh, wait.

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.940
They've all turned clear!

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:55.430
<i>The key!</i>

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.690
<i>Could this key be...</i>

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:02.170
<i>Release!</i>

00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:13.310
<i>It turned into a staff...</i>

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:21.930
<i>The incantation I've always used 
before won't do anything.</i>

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:25.180
<i>An incantation to let me use this staff...</i>

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:28.150
Sakura!

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:30.470
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:22:30.850 --> 00:22:34.150
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:22:35.590 --> 00:22:36.900
<i>Secure!</i>

00:22:55.490 --> 00:22:56.610
Sakura!

00:22:58.650 --> 00:22:59.940
What is that?

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:04.280
A new card...

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:09.820
<b>Gale</b>

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.300 --> 00:24:43.190
A mysterious incident and a new card.

00:24:43.190 --> 00:24:46.740
What? Tomoyo-chan, you made me a new costume?

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.760
Next time, "Sakura and the Room with No Exit."

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and the Room with No Exit</b>

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:55.010
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
